# Content
When editing Python files:
- Organise the imports in the standard order, so that ruff doesn't complain
- Favor native types instead of the typing library. Eg. use `dict` instead of `Dict`
- Only write comments when they're useful. Comments like `# Import models from the new models file` above an import statement are not useful since the import statement tells me the same information very legibly
